# JVM Common Native API

Configure the host-owned domain and connected adapter, then bind the trusted
tenant once with `SelectoEngine.configure(domain, adapter).withTenant(8)`.
The domain supplies `source.tenant_field`; fluent writes omit the matching
tenant assignment, while reads, actions and transaction callbacks inherit it.
Native Java, Kotlin and Scala facades share the same JVM engine lineage.

This notebook inspects and executes the committed Java sample on in-memory
SQLite. It requires the Java 21 toolchain selected by `selecto-jvm/mise.toml`,
`mise`, and the Gradle wrapper's dependencies. Set `SELECTO_JVM_PATH` if the
native checkout is not a sibling of `selecto_livebooks`. Verified native source:
`7fb922eb232097c73f3377e80761020a8abcfd7e`.

## Inspect The Native Java Program

```elixir
repo = System.get_env("SELECTO_JVM_PATH") || Path.expand("../../selecto-jvm", __DIR__)
source = Path.join(repo, "selecto-certification/src/main/java/io/selecto/certification/CommonNativeExample.java")
IO.puts(File.read!(source))
```

The sample supplies a native domain map, previews SQL with separately bound
parameters, inserts without `org_id`, and invokes the archive action through an
inherited transaction engine. A separate callback inserts another row, then
attempts a refused foreign-tenant delete; the earlier insert rolls back. The
final scoped read contains only `[2, 8, "Test", "archived"]`.

## Execute And Verify

```elixir
mise = System.find_executable("mise") || raise "mise executable is required"
{output, status} = System.cmd(mise, ["exec", "--", "./gradlew", "--quiet", ":selecto-certification:commonNativeExample"], cd: repo, stderr_to_stdout: true)
IO.puts(output)
if status != 0 or not String.contains?(output, "PASS common native API:"), do: raise "Native JVM sample failed"
```

The actual SQLite insert preview contains four `?` placeholders with parameters
`[2, "Test", "done", 8]`. The tenant stays in the SQL, even though assignments
omit it. `filter`, `expectedCardinality`, `returning`, conflict identity and query
enforcement retain native governance. Actions authorize afresh for preview and
execution; a preview never grants execution authority.

## Kotlin And Scala Calls

The idiomatic bindings use native maps and their typed domains/adapters:

```kotlin
val engine = SelectoEngine.configure(domain, adapter).withTenant(8)
engine.write().insert(mapOf("id" to 2, "name" to "Test"))
    .returning("id", "name").execute()
```

```scala
val engine = SelectoEngine.configure(domain, adapter).withTenant(8)
engine.write().insert(Map("id" -> 2, "name" -> "Test"))
  .returning("id", "name").execute()
```

Callbacks run synchronously and sequentially on the calling thread. Managed
work commits on success and rolls back on escaping failure. Nested work uses
native savepoints; host and external transactions keep their existing owner.
Callback engines and drafts expire when the callback ends. Custom adapters
without the transaction SPI explicitly refuse it.

Run `mise exec -- ./gradlew check` in the native checkout for regression tests.
The new Java storage scenarios run on SQLite and PostgreSQL; the latter needs a
disposable `SELECTO_JVM_POSTGRESQL_TEST_URL` in JDBC form. Kotlin/Scala native
binding tests execute their fluent calls on SQLite. This notebook does not claim
live coverage of other providers or arbitrary host action executors.
